    "reference": "The Preamble to the Constitution of India asserted that India is a secular nation following the 42nd Amendment in 1976. India does not have an official state religion, and the state is required to recognize and accept all religions. However, personal laws on marriage, divorce, and inheritance vary with an individual's religion, with Muslim Indians governed by Sharia-based Muslim Personal Law."
